      "blurb": "Aethlon Medical has agreed to merge with North Immunology, whose drug NOR-101 blocks two eczema signals, IL-13 and IL-18, in one antibody",
      "stance": "LONG",
      "status": "active",
      "initiated": "2026-09-23",
      "entry": 6.5,
      "summary": [
        "Eczema is not one disease: today's best drugs block the Th2 pathway, and many patients are driven only partly by it.",
        "Blocking IL-18 has worked in patients, including ones the Th2 drugs failed, and blocking it together with IL-13 should do more than either alone.",
        "NOR-101 does both in one long-lasting antibody, and could be the best eczema drug. It has not yet been given to a person.",
        "The shares are a way into North Immunology before it lists, at about the price large investors paid."
      ],
      "drivers": [
        "Three IL-18 blockers from other companies have worked in eczema patients.",
        "A half-life of about 42 days in monkeys, which points to a few injections a year.",
        "About $180M of new money, lasting into the second half of 2028, when the patient results are due."
      ],
      "risks": [
        "The merger may not close. Without it Aethlon is a shell with about $6.5M of cash.",
        "No trial has tested IL-13 and IL-18 together in people, and NOR-101 itself has only laboratory and monkey data.",
        "Talawar's TALA-125 blocks the same two signals, starts trials at the same time and has more money.",
        "The cash runs out about when the results arrive, so more shares will be sold."
      ],
