            "rows": [[["Fiserv (FISV): notes on the peer comparison",null,"b"],0],["How the comparison works and where it is weak.",0],[0,0],[["TOPIC",null,"b"],"NOTE"],[["Method",null,"b"],"Fiserv is compared with seven peers on price, debt and growth. A peer set's median multiple, applied to Fiserv's own earnings, gives a value per share for Fiserv."],[["Why more than P/E",null,"b"],"P/E says nothing about debt or growth. Two companies on the same P/E are not equally risky if one owes far more or is growing far slower. The Debt sheet and the closest-match peer set are there for that."],[["Peer sets",null,"b"],"Growth group: faster or slower than the sales growth line on the Inputs sheet (6% in 2027). Debt group: heavier or lighter than the net debt ÷ EBITDA line on the Inputs sheet (2.5 times). Closest match: peers in the same two groups as Fiserv."],[["Choosing peers",null,"b"],"Set a peer to 0 on the Inputs sheet to leave it out. To add one, insert a row inside the peer list on Inputs, Valuation and Debt and copy the formulas down."],[["EV/EBITDA",null,"b"],"Enterprise value (market value plus net debt) divided by EBITDA. Unlike P/E it counts the debt, so it is the fairer multiple for companies that owe very different amounts."],[["Debt measures",null,"b"],"Debt ÷ equity uses the equity on the balance sheet, which for Fiserv is after the $6.45bn goodwill write-down. Net debt ÷ EBITDA says how many years of cash earnings it would take to repay the debt. Interest cover says how many times those earnings cover the interest bill."],[["Deals in 2026",null,"b"],"Global Payments and FIS completed large deals on 12 Jan 2026, so their last 12 months cover about eight and a half months of the combined businesses. Their EBITDA is understated and their debt and EV/EBITDA ratios overstated."],[["EBITDA basis",null,"b"],"EBITDA here is on a reported basis less unusual items, the same for every company. Fiserv's own adjusted figure is higher, because it also leaves out its turnaround costs."],[["Jack Henry",null,"b"],"Its financial year ends in June. Its \"2026E\" is the year to June 2027 and its \"2027E\" the year to June 2028."],[["Shift4",null,"b"],"Its market value counts only its listed Class A shares, so its market value and enterprise value are understated. The P/E is not affected."],[["Estimates",null,"b"],"Earnings and sales growth are the average of analysts' estimates on each company's own adjusted basis. Adjusted earnings leave out costs each company treats as one-off."],[["Updating",null,"b"],"Change the boxed figures on the Inputs sheet and save. The site shows the new version at its next update."]],
