      "summary": [
        "Vaccines against WT1 have failed before, and REGAL was too small to measure the effect reliably. It passed with p = 0.035; one death in the other group would have pushed that past 0.05.",
        "SELLAS has not said whether the result counts every randomised patient. With numbers this small, one or two patients could decide it.",
        "The FDA will re-run the analysis itself. If real doubt remains, a refusal is a reasonable possibility, and the shares are worth the cash: $1.28.",
        "Even if approved, GPS is worth $1.54 to $5.54 a share on my model, against $19.15 on 17 Nov 2026."
      ],
      "drivers": [
        "The only blinded, randomised trial of a WT1 vaccine in AML, OCV-501, found no benefit (p = 0.77). A Phase 3 trial of another, DSP-7888, was stopped.",
        "REGAL could pass only by showing a cut of more than a third in the risk of death. A hazard ratio of 0.59 from 80 deaths would normally give p of about 0.02; the published 0.035 suggests the test drew on about 64 deaths' worth of information.",
        "The FDA approves on one trial when the result is very persuasive. p = 0.035 in 126 patients is not.",
        "About 3,200 patients a year in the US and Europe could get GPS. The price needs several billion dollars a year of sales at peak; my middle case is $394M."
      ],
