      "headline": "QBTS: FULL THESIS AND MODEL PUBLISHED; TARGET $2.73, TWICE CASH",
      "html": "<p>I have written up the case for being short D-Wave Quantum. At $9.56 the company is worth about $3.5bn. It sold $13M over the last four quarters and lost $48M in the latest one.</p><p>It rests on five beliefs: the price reflects belief in a revolution, not the business; D-Wave's machines cannot run Shor's algorithm; they have not been shown to beat ordinary computers at a job customers pay for; the business is a science project; and the shares are worth at most the cash.</p><p>Cash is $1.36 a share. I will close the short at twice that, $2.73, and work the figure out again after each quarter's results.</p>",
