      "headline": "FISV: PEER COMPARISON MODEL PUBLISHED; MID-TABLE ON PRICE, WEAK ON DEBT AND GROWTH",
      "html": "<p>The model compares Fiserv with seven peers instead of using a DCF. A P/E alone says nothing about business risk, so it also looks at debt, against both equity and earnings, and at growth.</p><p>Fiserv is fourth of the eight on price, at 8.8 times 2026 earnings and 8.2 times EV/EBITDA. It is seventh on debt to equity and last on 2026 sales growth. Only its margin stands out, second of the eight.</p><p>On its peers' multiples Fiserv is worth $49 to $56 a share against the slower growers and $109 to $161 against the faster ones, with the shares at $63.90. So the upside depends on the turnaround moving Fiserv into the faster group. I have not set a target.</p>",
