      "headline": "MRNA: INITIATING SHORT AT $247.12",
      "html": "<p>Moderna made its name with the COVID vaccine. Since August 2026 its value has rested mostly on one cancer drug, intismeran, which it shares with Merck.</p><p>I think the price assumes intismeran works in many cancers, not just melanoma. My model says the price needs intismeran to sell about $61bn a year at its peak. That is nearly twice what Keytruda, the biggest cancer drug, sold in 2025.</p><p>Melanoma alone is a small market for it, and Moderna keeps only half of what intismeran earns. Even if intismeran also succeeds after surgery in kidney, bladder and lung cancer, the model gives $45 to $61 a share.</p><p>The lung, kidney and bladder results are not known yet. Those results decide the short.</p>",
      "link": {
        "label": "Open MRNA thesis",
        "go": "#/s/MRNA/thesis"
      }
